CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ injected-class-name: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
does not uniquely resolve
--
In a class template with a constructor template, the injected-class-name
in sizeof(impl) and alignof(impl) resolved to the class and to its copy
constructor ("does not uniquely resolve").  Constructors have no names
([class.ctor.general]/1).  The MSVC STL's _Func_impl_no_alloc::_Delete_this
(std::function) lost its body this way.
